The timer lets the tick pass at which the running share's account drains or fills.
A share alone on the processor would run on its account past the tick that leaves it less than a tick;
the tick the turn's account drains or fills is not one the timer lets pass.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-grain32 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: the timer lets the tick pass that drains the turn's account

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -480,7 +480,8 @@ uint32_t sched_wake_ticks(void)
         return 1;
     }
     uint32_t change = share_change(turn, balance, drained);
-    return change < wake ? change : wake;
+    (void)change;
+    return wake;
 }
 
 bool sched_interrupt(uint32_t line)
